:false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.40128122445458614,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.09516391388609763,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":1.6,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.07567369543192326,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":62.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.017759510225004004,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":32.2,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.020287579536618954,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.15485695030371294,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.03488700152740079,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":41.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.02172,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":14.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.5,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":50.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Orthofix Medical Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as a medical technology company in the United States, Italy, the United Kingdom, France, Germany, Brazil, and internationally. It operates through two segments, Global Spine and Global Limb Reconstruction. The Global Spine segment manufactures, distributes, and provides support services for bone growth stimulation devices that enhance bone fusion; designs, develops, and markets a portfolio of spine fixation implant products for use throughout the spinal column; and offers bone graft substitutes, such as fiber-based and particulate demineralized bone matrices, cellular bone allografts, collagen ceramic matrices, and synthetic bone void fillers in various forms with supporting graft delivery solutions to treat various spinal, orthopedic, and dental conditions. This segment also designs, develops, and markets a portfolio of navigation technologies, including tracked surgical tools, intelligent software, and imaging equipment based on machine-vision and optical innovations; and 7D FLASH Navigation System, a navigation platform for spinal and cranial procedures. The Global Limb Reconstruction segment offers products and solutions for the underserved limb reconstruction market, including deformity correction, limb lengthening, complex fracture management, and limb preservation. This segment also designs, develops, and markets external and internal fixation limb reconstruction products that are coupled with enabling digital technologies to support the entire patient care continuum. It sells its products through distributors and sales representatives to hospitals, healthcare organizations, healthcare providers, ambulatory surgery centers, and out-patient hospitals. The company was formerly known as Orthofix International N.V. and changed its name to Orthofix Medical Inc. in July 2018. Orthofix Medical Inc. was founded in 1980 and is headquartered in Lewisville, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Massimo  Calafiore | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $512K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $18K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Orthofix Medical Inc. is a micro-cap healthcare business with a $292M market cap on $822M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +21% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -14% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 75% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $1M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -4.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 2.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 68/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"News sentiment running negative (-0.11) across recent coverage","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_ta